I found a real CaveVines gap in addition to the copper hook gaps: the shared Rust implementation treated the head like the plant body during bone-meal use. Vanilla’s head inherits `GrowingPlantHeadBlock.performBonemeal`, which grows one segment; the body alone sets berries. I’m correcting that live `perform_bonemeal` caller while preserving the existing random-growth path.
apply patch
