I found one genuine live gap: vanilla `JukeboxBlock.setPlacedBy` sets `HAS_RECORD` when a placed jukebox item carries `RecordItem` (`JukeboxBlock.java:45-51`). Pumpkin already applies the item’s block-entity data, but no jukebox placement callback updates the block state, so placed jukeboxes can contain a record while remaining `HAS_RECORD=false`. I’m wiring this through the existing `player_placed` dispatch and adding a pure state-transition test.
