codex
The interaction-shape lead is also genuine, not client-only: vanilla’s `BlockGetter` uses `getInteractionShape` during server raycasts (`BlockGetter.java:84-90`), while Pumpkin’s raycast currently only uses generated outline shapes. I’m adding the hopper’s five-direction interaction geometry and wiring it into the existing synchronous raycast, including the vanilla “override only when the interaction hit is closer” rule.
apply patch
