    39	    /// `TargetingConditions.test` (`targeting/TargetingConditions.java:64-97`) for the
    40	    /// non-combat conditions that `Sensor.isEntityTargetable` uses
    41	    /// (`sensing/Sensor.java:16,66-70`): the combat-only branches do not apply, so the test
    42	    /// is `canBeSeenByAnyone` + the visibility-modified range check + line of sight. The
    43	    /// shared-static range mutation from `Sensor.updateTargetingConditionRanges`
    44	    /// (`sensing/Sensor.java:52-60`) is folded in as the `follow_range` parameter instead.
    45	    async fn is_targetable(
    46	        mob_entity: &MobEntity,
    47	        observer_type: &EntityType,
    48	        follow_range: f64,
    49	        distance_sq: f64,
