codex
The audit found one real behavioral gap: 26.2’s move packets carry a horizontal-collision flag, and the current Java handlers parse only the old ground/in-wall byte and never store that flag on the player. I’ll update all four serverbound movement packet variants and wire the value into the existing atomic entity state. The sensor and skull leads have live Rust equivalents or client-only behavior, so I won’t add dead methods for them.
