    72	/// The block-level surface every worldgen feature actually uses.
    73	///
    74	/// Vanilla features run against a `WorldGenLevel` (`Feature.place` takes a
    75	/// `FeaturePlaceContext` whose `level()` is one), an interface a live `ServerLevel`
    76	/// implements just as `WorldGenRegion` does; no feature reaches for a chunk object. This
    77	/// trait mirrors that split deliberately: it mentions no [`ProtoChunk`], so a runtime
    78	/// adapter backed by a live world can implement it and drive feature placement -
    79	/// bone-mealed moss and nylium, sapling growth - without synthesising proto chunks.
    80	///
    81	/// Chunk-graph access, which exists only while a chunk is being generated, lives in
    82	/// [`ProtoChunkCache`].
