codex
The three leads are mostly already represented by live Rust machinery: dark-oak methods are translated into the existing foliage dispatch/validator, advancement accessors are client-consumer-only, and creaking-heart update/removal hooks are handled by `chunk_data_nbt`, `update_block_entity`, and `on_block_replaced`. I found one concern worth closing in code: the creaking binding setter currently has no caller, so I’m tracing the existing spawn/registration APIs before deciding whether a source-faithful live wiring is possible.
